tags: proof-of-work, pow

A kind of network: the nodes of one proof-of-work blockchain that are on one chain. A
member is a node of the chain, as it reports its own state. The node does not verify
the proof of work.

The value is key=value lines, sorted by key, separated by a newline. The required keys
are pow.chain (the name of the chain, for example ergo), pow.block_id (a block, in
lowercase hexadecimal) and pow.min_cumulative_difficulty (the work since the genesis
block, base 10). The optional keys are pow.min_height (base 10) and pow.max_tip_age_s
(seconds, base 10). Another key is not valid.

A member reports that its main chain contains pow.block_id, that its cumulative
difficulty is at least pow.min_cumulative_difficulty, that its height is at least
pow.min_height, and that its last block is not older than pow.max_tip_age_s. A node
that cannot resolve the chain refuses. The node is bound.

=== formal
check=what each node reports about its own chain; the proof of work is not verified
class=domain
members=the nodes of the chain pow.chain whose main chain contains pow.block_id, with a cumulative difficulty of at least pow.min_cumulative_difficulty, a height of at least pow.min_height and a last block not older than pow.max_tip_age_s
name=proof-of-work
value=key=value lines sorted by key: pow.chain, pow.block_id (lowercase hexadecimal), pow.min_cumulative_difficulty (base 10) are required; pow.min_height (base 10) and pow.max_tip_age_s (seconds, base 10) are optional; no other key
